<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Allied-occupied Germany</h1><p class="st-meta">1945 CE – 1949 CE · capital Berlin</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Defeated Germany under the rule of the four Allied powers, divided into zones that grew into two German states.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany's</a> unconditional surrender in May 1945, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin-declaration-1945">Berlin Declaration</a> of 5 June 1945 transferred supreme authority to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a>, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a>, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">United Kingdom</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. Germany was divided into four occupation zones, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a> into four sectors, and the lands east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oder-neisse-line">Oder-Neisse line</a> passed to Polish and Soviet administration.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Allied Control Council coordinated policy under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/potsdam-agreement">Potsdam Agreement</a>: denazification, demilitarisation, democratisation and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-reparations">reparations</a>. The major Nazi leaders were tried at <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-imperial-city-of-nuremberg">Nuremberg</a>. Millions of Germans expelled from the east had to be resettled. Cooperation broke down as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cold-war">Cold War</a> began: the western zones introduced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deutsche-mark">Deutsche Mark</a> in 1948, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviets</a> blockaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-berlin">West Berlin</a>, answered by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin-airlift">Berlin Airlift</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In May 1949 the western zones became the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/federal-republic-of-germany">Federal Republic of Germany</a>, and in October 1949 the Soviet zone became the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-germany">German Democratic Republic</a>. Allied rights over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> as a whole ended only with reunification in 1990.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="other, 1945 CE – 1949 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 64 H80 L70 78 H30 Z"/><path d="M50 64 V18"/><path d="M50 22 L72 56 H50"/><path d="M50 28 L32 56 H50"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">other</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Germany and Central Europe</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:98.41%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1945 CE – 1949 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Berlin</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Lucius D. Clay, Georgy Zhukov</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Lutheranism, Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Occupied Germany, Allied Control Council</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1947&amp;focus=allied-occupied-germany" aria-label="Allied-occupied Germany on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4980 366 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Allied-occupied Germany lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5300 622L5300 622M5300 622L5227 665"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5300 622h0M5227 665h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5300 622h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5300 622h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Berlin. <a href="/atlas?year=1947&amp;focus=allied-occupied-germany">On the atlas &r